@page
@model PrivacyModel
@{ ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy"; }

<div class="page-head"><h1>Privacy</h1></div>

<div class="panel pad stack" style="max-width: 46em; gap: 20px;">
    <p>Quotebook is a portfolio demo by Adriel Tang, not a commercial service. Please don't enter real customer, banking or personal details.</p>

    <div>
        <h2>What is stored</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>If you create an account: your name, email address and a hashed password (the password itself is never stored).</li>
            <li>Whatever you type into the app: customers, quotations, invoices and payments.</li>
            <li>A cookie that keeps you signed in, and a security cookie that protects forms. There is no advertising or analytics tracking, and the fonts are served from this site, not a third party.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div>
        <h2>Who can see it</h2>
        <p>Other users of the app can't see your data. The data lives in a PostgreSQL database hosted on Neon, and the app runs on Render. As the person running the demo, I can technically read the database, so treat anything you enter as visible to me.</p>
    </div>

    <div>
        <h2>The demo business</h2>
        <p>The "Try the demo" account is shared by every visitor. Its data is sample data and is wiped and refilled every 6 hours.</p>
    </div>

    <div>
        <h2>Deleting your data</h2>
        <p>To have an account and its data removed, email <a href="mailto:adrieltangte@gmail.com">adrieltangte@gmail.com</a>.</p>
    </div>
</div>
